implementationPlan.description:
docs/RELEASING.md, section 1 'Bump versions'. Its list names exactly the fields the guard checks, in the guard's order:
- the four packages' package.json and package-lock.json (top-level `version` and `packages[""].version`);
- packages/moe-claude-plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json (`version`);
- moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts (`version = "X.Y.Z"`);
- installer/moe-installer.iss (`AppVersion=X.Y.Z`).

Add one sentence after the list. The session mods' own scripts/mods/*/.claude-plugin/plugin.json files keep their own versions. They ship inside both IDE plugin bundles (scripts/bundle-manifest.json) and are never released on their own, so the guard does not check them.

Section 2 keeps its text: the guard prints PASS, and the workflow stops on a mismatch, which is now true for every listed field. Edit with the editing tool. Docs-only, so no test runs here.
